          {
            "title": "Lines of code",
            "id": 129295,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Programs are more fun if they can take input from the outside.</p><p>When we run code, we can include the input to alter the program.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Order",
            "id": 129296,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The order of the instructions matters. Once we collect input and store it in a variable, we can reuse it.</p><p>Put the lines in the right order to use the collected output in the output statement.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"name_input = input()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi, \" /><text value=\"{name_input}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"75\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"What's your name?\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Hi, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>name_input = input()</code>, followed by <code>print(f\"Hi, {name_input}!\")</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The order of instructions matters. Use <code>input()</code> to collect a reply, then store it in a variable to reuse it.</p><p>Order the lines to ask <code>What's your name?</code>, store the reply, then greet the user.</p><p>For input <code>Mimo</code>, print <code>Hi, Mimo!</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"name_input = input()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi, \" /><text value=\"{name_input}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"26\" /><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"75\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"input() = name_input\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print(f&quot;Hi, name_input!&quot;)\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"What's your name?\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Hi, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>print(\"What's your name?\")</code>, followed by <code>name_input = input()</code>, and finally <code>print(f\"Hi, {name_input}!\")</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Console",
            "id": 129297,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To gather input from a user in a Python program, we use the <code>input</code> function. The user's input can then be assigned to a variable.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input()\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>input</code>, followed by <code>(</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To gather input from a user in a Python program, we use the <code>input</code> function. The user's input can then be assigned to a variable.</p><p>Store one reply from the user in <code>user_input</code>, without printing it yet.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input()\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"12\" /><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"output\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>user_input</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, <code>input</code>, <code>(</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Displaying multiple times",
            "id": 129298,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>After capturing input, we can assign it to a variable and use it just as any other variable.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"user_input = input()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi, \" /><text value=\"{user_input}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"37\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"What's your name?\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Hi, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>user_input</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Ask <code>What's your name?</code>, store the reply, and use it so input <code>Mimo</code> prints <code>Hi, Mimo!</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"user_input = input()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi, \" /><text value=\"{user_input}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"name = input()\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"{name_input}\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;user_input&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"What's your name?\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Hi, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>user_input = input()</code>, followed by <code>{user_input}</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Prompt",
            "id": 129551,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can also add an additional prompt to the <code>input</code> function. The prompt will be displayed in the console.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your name: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"38\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Enter your name: \" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"Enter your name: \"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can also add an additional prompt to the <code>input</code> function. The prompt will be displayed in the console.</p><p>Complete the line so it shows the exact prompt <code>Enter your name: </code> and stores what the user types in <code>user_input</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your name: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"38\" /><option startIndex=\"38\" endIndex=\"39\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Enter your name: \" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>input</code>, followed by <code>(</code>, <code>\"Enter your name: \"</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Output",
            "id": 129300,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If we enter an additional prompt, the user will start typing at the same line as the prompt is displayed in the console.</p><p>That's why it's helpful to add a whitespace at the end of the prompt used in the <code>input</code> function.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your name: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(f\" /><text value=\"&quot;Thanks, {user_input}!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Enter your name: Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Thanks, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Output - Copy",
            "id": 129552,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can use the <code>input</code> function as many times as we want.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input_1 = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter a number: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"user_input_2 = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter another number: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(user_input_1)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(user_input_2)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Enter a number: 100\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Enter another number: 200\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"100\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"200\" /></content></output></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Numbers",
            "id": 129553,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The input is always of type string. If we want to use it as a number, we need to convert it to an integer or float beforehand.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input_1 = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter a number: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"user_input_2 = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter another number: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"number1 = int(user_input_1)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"number2 = int(user_input_2)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"result = number1 + number2\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(f\" /><text value=\"&quot;The sum is {result}&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Enter a number: 100\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Enter another number: 200\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"The sum is 300\" /></content></output></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 1",
            "id": 129301,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the type of the input we capture?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"false\">The input from the user is either a string or a number</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"true\">All input from the user is treated as a string</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">All input from the user is treated as a string.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A user types <code>42</code> after an <code>input()</code> call. What type is stored before any conversion?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"false\">A number, because <code>42</code> only contains digits</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"true\">A string, because captured input starts as text</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">A string or a number, depending on what the user types</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A string, because captured input starts as text.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 2",
            "id": 129302,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What do we use the <code>input</code> function for?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">To receive input from the user</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">To produce output for the user</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">To receive input from the user.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The <code>input</code> function receives input from the user.</p><p>A program asks the user for their city. Which job belongs to <code>input()</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Read the user's typed answer so the program can use it</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Display the city on the screen for the user to read</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Convert the user's answer to the type the program needs</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Read the user's typed answer so the program can use it.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 3",
            "id": 129303,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does the <code>input()</code> function do?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It reads a line from input and returns it as a string</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It writes a value to output</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It reads a line from input and returns it as a string.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>After the user presses Enter, what does <code>input()</code> return to the program?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The line the user typed, as a string</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A message written to the console output</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The line as a number when it contains only digits</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The line the user typed, as a string.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 4",
            "id": 129304,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What will the output be, assuming an input of <code>10</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"age_string = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your age: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (int(age_string) &lt; \" /><text value=\"21\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"):\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Under 21&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"else\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;21 or older&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Enter your age: 10\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Under 21\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>Under 21</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>21 or older</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>Under 21</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The <code>if</code> block runs when its condition is <code>True</code>. Otherwise, the <code>else</code> block runs.</p><p>The output shown is for input <code>10</code>. If the user types <code>21</code> instead, which final line will the code display?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"age_string = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your age: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (int(age_string) &lt; \" /><text value=\"21\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"):\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Under 21&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"else\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;21 or older&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Enter your age: 10\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Under 21\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>21 or older</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>Under 21</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>21</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>21 or older</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example 1",
            "id": 129305,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Ask the user for their name and store it in the variable <code>user_name</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_name = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your name: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"17\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>input</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Store the answer from the prompt <code>Enter your name: </code> in <code>user_name</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_name = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your name: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"9\" /><option startIndex=\"10\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"37\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"name\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>user_name</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, <code>input</code>, and finally <code>\"Enter your name: \"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
